{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01224",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 4.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.75,
      "end_seconds": 10.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "So, yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.4,
      "end_seconds": 16.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Doctor, it's heartburn most days. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.29,
      "end_seconds": 21.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Okay, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.56,
      "end_seconds": 25.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "It's been going on for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.43,
      "end_seconds": 28.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Does anything set it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.48,
      "end_seconds": 31.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "It's worse with large meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.66,
      "end_seconds": 38.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.35,
      "end_seconds": 42.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.03,
      "end_seconds": 46.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.15,
      "end_seconds": 55.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "It usually comes with a sour taste. With sour taste, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.98,
      "end_seconds": 73.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Have you had any vomiting, black stools, weight loss or chest pain on exertion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.52,
      "end_seconds": 82.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting, black stools, weight loss or chest pain on exertion, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.97,
      "end_seconds": 92.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Right, any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.91,
      "end_seconds": 94.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.01,
      "end_seconds": 106.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.12,
      "end_seconds": 110.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.62,
      "end_seconds": 123.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.26,
      "end_seconds": 131.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.57,
      "end_seconds": 137.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Alright, any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.57,
      "end_seconds": 146.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "No, nothing I can think of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.06,
      "end_seconds": 150.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Any regular medication, tablets or creams?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 153.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.38,
      "end_seconds": 156.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.52,
      "end_seconds": 159.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.0,
      "end_seconds": 164.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.69,
      "end_seconds": 171.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.95,
      "end_seconds": 176.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "So, I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.91,
      "end_seconds": 185.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.59,
      "end_seconds": 208.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.4 degrees, blood pressure 120 over 82, heart rate 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.52,
      "end_seconds": 212.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.41,
      "end_seconds": 218.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.48,
      "end_seconds": 223.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.91,
      "end_seconds": 231.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.55,
      "end_seconds": 234.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.28,
      "end_seconds": 256.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild tenderness at the top."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.38,
      "end_seconds": 261.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.43,
      "end_seconds": 291.38,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. It's hard to say. Reflux with a swallowing symptom that needs a camera test is one possibility and a narrowing of the gullet another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.28,
      "end_seconds": 294.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.42,
      "end_seconds": 312.54,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like reflux with a swallowing symptom that needs a camera test, but I'd like to confirm. I'm sending you for a blood count because of reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.61,
      "end_seconds": 316.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.45,
      "end_seconds": 321.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "We should do an endoscopy for dysphagia and reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.41,
      "end_seconds": 324.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Mm, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.27,
      "end_seconds": 345.57,
      "duration_seconds": 19.3,
      "text": "You'll be taking omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, four weeks. That should help with reflux. Eat smaller meals and avoid eating for three hours before bed. The gastroenterology clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.34,
      "end_seconds": 347.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.03,
      "end_seconds": 366.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.52,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. I'll want another look after the endoscopy. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.05,
      "end_seconds": 378.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "So, I take the omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day and come back after the endoscopy. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.88,
      "end_seconds": 384.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. So, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.36,
      "end_seconds": 388.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.73,
      "end_seconds": 391.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}